<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Temenos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Temenos was, in Greek myth, a great-great-grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heracles">Heracles</a> who led the return of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heracleidae">Heracleidae</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> and received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> as his share. The kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argead-dynasty">Argeads</a>, claimed descent from him, which allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a> to be accepted as a Greek at the Olympic Games. He was said to have been killed by his own sons.</p></div>
